@startuml

!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #1A73E8
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #1A73E8
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #F0F6FF

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #EBF3FB
  BorderColor #1A73E8
  FontName Arial
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #2E4057
}

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #2E4057
  BorderColor #1F1F1F
  FontColor #FFFFFF
  FontName Arial
  FontSize 12
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F59E0B
  FontName Arial
  FontSize 11
}

skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #1A73E8
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor #D6E8FA
skinparam ActivationBorderColor #1A73E8

title Diagramme de séquence — Marquer comme lue et naviguer

actor "Chef de chantier" as User

participant "NotificationDialog\n/ AlertsPageComponent" as Dialog
participant "AlertService\n(Angular)" as Service
participant "Angular Router\n+ localStorage" as Router

== Consultation d'une alerte ==

User -> Dialog : 1. Clic sur l’alerte
activate Dialog

Dialog -> Service : 2. markAsRead(alert.id)
activate Service

Service -> Service : 3. readAlertIds.add(alert.id)

Service -> Router : 4. localStorage.setItem(...)

Router --> Service : Confirmation sauvegarde

Service -> Service : 5. alertsSubject.next(...)\nBadge recalculé

== Navigation vers l'entité ==

Dialog -> Service : 6. navigateToAlert(alert)

Service -> Service : 7. routes[alert.type] -> route

Service -> Router : 8. router.navigate([route], {highlight})

Router --> User : 9. Navigation vers composant cible

Dialog --> User : 10. dialogRef.close()

deactivate Service
deactivate Dialog

== Action optionnelle ==

opt Marquer toutes les alertes comme lues

    Dialog -> Service : markAllAsRead()
    activate Service

    Service -> Service : Toutes les alertes\najoutées à readAlertIds

    Service -> Router : localStorage.setItem(...)

    Router --> Service : Confirmation

    Service -> Service : alertsSubject.next(...)\nBadge = 0

    deactivate Service

end

note right of Service
Le service :
- conserve les IDs lus
- met à jour le badge
- déclenche la navigation
- persiste les données
dans localStorage
end note

@enduml